# Welcome to the Country Searcher Project

**Project by Axel Lima**  
**For DevelopsToday**

This project is a **test vacancy project** created for evaluating the skills and knowledge of developers at **DevelopsToday**. It allows users to search for countries and explore country-related data.

The project is split into two main parts:

- The **front-end** where users interact with the application.
- The **back-end** which handles data fetching and processing from external APIs.

## Project Structure

The project is divided into two sections:

1. **[Front-end](./front-end)**: The user-facing application where users can search for countries.
2. **[Back-end](./back-end)**: The server-side application that fetches data from external APIs.

## Getting Started

To get started, you'll need to clone the repository and set up both the front-end and back-end applications.

### 1. Clone the repository

Start by cloning the repository to your local machine:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Axeellima/test-developstoday
cd test-developstoday
```
````

### 2. Set up the **Front-end**

Navigate to the `front-end` folder and follow the instructions in the **[Front-end README](./front-end/README.md)**:

```bash
cd front-end
```

This will guide you on how to configure and start the front-end application.

### 3. Set up the **Back-end**

Navigate to the `back-end` folder and follow the instructions in the **[Back-end README](./back-end/README.md)**:

```bash
cd back-end
```

This will guide you on how to configure and start the back-end API.

---

Once you've completed the setup for both parts, you can run the application and start exploring countries!

---

## Technologies Used

- **Front-end**: React, Chakra UI
- **Back-end**: Node.js, Express.js

---

Thank you for checking out this test vacancy project, created by **Axel Lima** for **DevelopsToday**!
